The gate machinery, the canonical decision serialization, and the two generic
reference checks (secrets, allowlist) were extracted from the Open Agentic
Platform (OAP), `crates/policy-kernel/lib.rs`, where they carry an SPDX header
reading `AGPL-3.0-or-later`. Relicensing this extracted source to Apache-2.0 is
the prerogative of the sole copyright holder (Bartek Kus) and is an explicit,
authorized act.

This is the Case-B extraction: OAP's `evaluate()` hardcoded six checks in a
fixed order over a code-governance-shaped `ToolCallContext`. The generic library
keeps the outcome enum, the pure-function property, and the canonical
serialization, and lifts the check set into a pluggable `Check` registry over a
domain-neutral `ActionContext`. OAP's four domain checks (destructive-op,
spec-status, spec-risk, diff-size) are NOT in this library; they stay in OAP as
registered checks. Only the two genuinely domain-neutral checks (secrets
scanning, action allowlist) are shipped here, behind the optional `checks-common`
feature. OAP's `PolicyBundle` / `PolicyRule` config model is not adopted; checks
self-configure.

Reproducible decision hashing rests on `canonical-keysort-json`, itself
extracted and relicensed Apache-2.0 from OAP's `crates/canonical-json`.

A forthcoming OAP extraction spec (analogous to spec 219 for tenant-tail)
formalizes the vend; the interim record is
`chancery/docs/preliminary/00-extraction-overview.md` and `02-action-gate.md`.
